      "learned": "A rotation turns every point about a fixed centre through the same angle in the same direction. Distances from the centre, lengths, angles, shape and size stay the same, so the image is congruent to the object. Only the position and the direction the figure faces change. Positive angles are anticlockwise and negative angles are clockwise.",
      "explained": "Kenya feels still but turns with Earth about its axis. Because rotation preserves distances, shape and size, Nairobi, Mombasa and Kisumu keep their distances from the axis and from one another as they turn anticlockwise together, which helps explain why the day-night pattern repeats regularly. The turning is described with a centre (Earth's axis), an angle and a direction."
