        "teacherMoves": "Say: 'Which question on our board can we now answer, and what is the evidence?' WAIT TIME of 10-15 seconds. Cold-call 4 learners to read and place a note. Say: 'Which questions need Lesson 4's grids and which need our globe model?' Point to Otieno's question about dawn at Mombasa and say: 'We now have the 15° per hour tool to calculate this later.' Do not answer all questions: leave the Mombasa-before-Kisumu timing open for Lesson 9.",
        "sensemakingStrategy": "Driving Question Board (DQB) with question clustering. Seeing questions move from 'open' to 'answered by evidence' shows learners that the mathematics is advancing the driving question 'what makes day and night possible?' Clustering questions helps learners decide what evidence is still needed.",
        "formativeAssessment": "Count new questions that involve the centre, angle or direction. Check that learners cite specific evidence (the bisector meeting point, 6 hours for 90°). Note whether questions show progress, for example from 'Why does the Sun move?' to 'How many degrees does Earth turn between Mombasa dawn and Nairobi midday?'"
